 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the YARS1 gene and its association with Charcot–Marie–Tooth disease. YARS1 is linked to tyrosyl-tRNA synthetase and has variants E196K, E196Q, G41R, and D81I. It is also associated with CMTDIC, which has a growth defect in a humanized yeast model. The gene is expressed in Escherichia coli and has a canonical function related to ARSs. Additionally, the cluster includes various methods and tools, such as GraphPad Prism, One-way ANOVA, and microscope imaging, which are used to study the gene and disease.",
